  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "Let $I=[0,1]\u2282R$ and ${X}_{i}=[-2i,2i]\\times [-i,i].$ Which of the following represents ${\u22c2}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{\u22c2}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[-1,1]\\times [-0.5,0.5]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [-1,1],b\\in [-0.5,0.5]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(-1,-0.5),$ $(-1,0.5),$ $(1,0.5),$ and $(1,-0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/0a3f27ff85f8a5b56e912f33976846b36fc90d35a87201c146c5345f4e31ba46.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[-2i,2i]\\times [-i,i]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [-2i,2i],b\\in [-i,i]}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(-2i,-i),$ $(-2i,i),$ $(2i,i),$ and $(2i,-i).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/d32279c2279fe234accaae96e5abc86a122adf60dc930c5e299b2f0c2db0028e.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the point $(0,0):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/4fdd8fc71b47304bb87e2d70a229bc0a545f85f0fe268d79036884421ed3765e.png)",
